# Mailpit preflight for comprehensive messaging tests (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08-05): during “comprehensive” Playwright testing,
agents **never started Mailpit**, did not notice it was down, and still
reported messaging pages as PASS. They never exercised email send,
template replaceable arguments, event→notification mail, or
approver-pending-request email. RCA:
`pim-offline-server/docs/dev/mailpit-comprehensive-test-gap-rca-20260805.md`.

## The rule

> **When the operator asks for a comprehensive / full / all-pages
> product test of AIC Server (or any messaging, email, event-
> notification, or approval-email coverage), Mailpit (or the
> configured lab SMTP catcher) MUST be Running and reachable before
> that coverage is claimed. Agents MUST exercise a real send path,
> template + placeholder/replaceable arguments, and at least one
> event-driven notification OR approver-pending-request email with
> the message visible in the catcher inbox. Page-load / nav-crawl /
> heading-only evidence is forbidden as “messaging tested.”**

## When this rule applies

Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive): comprehensive test, full product
test, all-pages / admin crawl “complete,” messaging tested, email
tested, templates tested, event notifications tested, approver /
pending-request email tested, AIC Server e2e suite covering Settings
→ Messaging.

Does **not** force Mailpit for pure layout chrome work that
explicitly scopes out send/notify (still must not claim messaging
workflows tested).

## Required preflight (before claiming coverage)

1. **Start** (if not already Running):
   `pwsh c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-server\scripts\Start-LabSmtpSink.ps1`
2. **Point Messaging → Email** at the sink when needed:
   `pwsh c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-server\scripts\Configure-LabSmtpMessaging.ps1`
3. **Prove reachability:**
   `GET http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/info` succeeds (SMTP
   `127.0.0.1:1025`, UI/API `:8025` — see
   `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/lab-smtp-sink.md`).
4. If the catcher is down: **start it or mark messaging/email/
   approval-notification coverage blocked** — do not PASS the
   surface on chrome alone.

Keep lab services alone unless the task needs this preflight or a
documented restore. Never rotate `phil`. No `cargo clean`.

## Required exercises (minimum set)

Before claiming messaging / email / approvals coverage, complete
**all** of:

| # | Exercise | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Send path** | Messaging test send and/or API `/api/offline/messaging/email/test` (or equivalent) succeeds |
| 2 | **Template + replaceable args** | Template (or snippet) with placeholders rendered; body/subject shows substituted values (not raw `{placeholder}` only) |
| 3 | **Event notify OR approver mail** | At least one: anomalous/event-driven notification **or** approver-pending-request / approval deep-link email |
| 4 | **Inbox observation** | Message visible in Mailpit UI or `GET http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/messages` (subject / To / body fragment) |

Soft-pass patterns that still green when SMTP is unconfigured (e.g.
TOD four-eyes accepting `smtp_unconfigured`) are **not** comprehensive
messaging coverage.

## Forbidden constructs

- Claiming messaging / email / templates / event notifications /
  approver mail “tested” from nav crawl, menu crawl, or heading
  asserts on `/messaging`, `/messaging/templates`,
  `/messaging/snippets`, `/messaging/email`, `/messaging/sms`,
  `/events/*`, or `/pam/approver-profile` alone.
- Skipping Mailpit preflight, then reporting comprehensive PASS.
- Treating connectivity-probe step logs alone as inbox delivery
  proof without a catcher message.
- Inventing docker-compose Mailpit when the lab contract is
  `Start-LabSmtpSink.ps1` (winget process on loopback).

